id: bluetooth_agents_host
label: Bluetooth host agents.md contributions
package: bluetooth_le_host
description: >
  Bluetooth Host API usage contributions for agents.md
category: Bluetooth|Bluetooth Host (Stack)
quality: evaluation
provides:
- name: bluetooth_agents_host
template_contribution:
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_stack
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_stack
    context: |
      # Bluetooth Host for Silicon Labs Series 2 and Series 3 devices on SiSDK
      - API details live in this SiSDK's Bluetooth Stack API header `sl_bt_*.h`.
        Consult them when needed.
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_feature_advertiser
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_feature_advertiser_host
    context: |
      ## Advertising (host BGAPI)
      - Different advertising types can be enabled on the same set created from
       `sl_bt_advertiser_create_set()`.
      - Type-specific advertising has own APIs setting data and start; stop legacy/extended
        with `sl_bt_advertiser_stop()`; periodic/PAwR with their own `stop` API.
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_feature_gatt_server
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_feature_gatt_server
    context: |
      ## GATT server
      - `user`-type characteristics require application responses to
        `sl_bt_evt_gatt_server_user_read_request`, and to
        `sl_bt_evt_gatt_server_user_write_request` if the `att_opcode` is not
        `sl_bt_gatt_write_command`. When `att_opcode` is `sl_bt_gatt_write_command`,
        do not send an ATT response. Missing a required response times out the GATT procedure.
      - Indications need confirmation before the next on a connection; no
        confirmation will time out the GATT.

ui_hints:
  visibility: never

metadata:
  sbom:
    license: MSLA
root_path: bluetooth_le_host
